## Phase gates (order of integration, not absolute sequence of all rows)

| Phase | Gate | Readiness rules |
|---|---|---|
| F0. Reconcile | R00 + R01 critical review | 203/203 mapping, no unsafe active exposure; single integrator main |
| F1. Canonical trust | R02 + R08 + selected R09/R11/R12 | Source/permissions, AI off, original Radio API preserved |
| F2. Clear experiences | R03–R07 + R06 | Real navigation/status and same shared domain contracts |
| F3. Governed publication | R09–R10 | Human approvals, rights, withdrawal, public projections |
| F4. Controlled migration | R13 subset | ARSY physical rename only when isolation/rollback evidence exists |
| F5. RC/Release | R13 release gate | CI, browser, security, backup and explicit go/no-go on same SHA |

## Anti-overlap rules

**Dock** displays released/public data; **Headquarters** handles humans/content/governance; **Cockpit** controls local runtime only. **ARSY** is the single backend; **MoonUI** owns shared visual semantics. **Research** owns research states; **Governance** owns public release; **Corpus** owns source rights; **Story** owns fiction; **Witness** owns personal testimony; **Journey** owns voluntary mandates, not privileged operation. **AI Gateway** serves model transport, not authority; **Sentinel** collects, never publishes autonomously. No new API or workspace solely because a label is newly named.

